<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 3 November, from 361 to 1957.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantius-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">361 <span class="tih-ago">1,665 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantius II dies, leaving Julian sole emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Constantius II died in Cilicia while marching against his cousin Julian, who became sole Roman emperor. Julian, the last pagan emperor, tried to revive traditional cults but was killed fighting Persia in 363.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1492 <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VII and Charles VIII make peace at Étaples</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Peace of Étaples ended Henry VII's brief invasion of France: Charles VIII paid him a large sum and agreed to stop supporting Yorkist pretenders. The treaty helped secure the new Tudor dynasty.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1793 <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Olympe de Gouges is guillotined</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The playwright Olympe de Gouges, author of the Declaration of the Rights of Woman and of the Female Citizen, was executed during the Terror for writings attacking the Jacobins.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-opium-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1839 <span class="tih-ago">187 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British and Chinese warships clash at Chuenpi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Royal Navy frigates fought Chinese war junks off Chuenpi near Canton, the first major clash of the First Opium War. The dispute followed Lin Zexu's destruction of British merchants' opium; China lost Hong Kong in 1842.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soviet-union.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1957 <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Laika becomes the first animal to orbit the Earth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet Union launched the dog Laika aboard Sputnik 2. She died within hours from overheating, but the flight showed a living creature could survive launch and weightlessness.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
